# Lesson 02 of the Plasm Koans. Each row is one koan: what the learner discovers,
# and the acceptance scenario of Plasm it teaches (feature: scenario).
Feature: What a repo is
  Every koan is given repo, a Plasm repository over the koans database. A repo runs queries and writes against one database with one model. A query is only a description: the repo turns it into SQL, sends it when asked, and returns a Result.

  Prerequisites: lesson 01.

  Background:
    Given the koans database with its starting data

  Scenario Outline: <koan>
    Given the koan "<koan>" in this lesson
    Then it passes with its reference answer and fails until its blanks are filled
    And it teaches the acceptance scenario "<teaches>"

    Examples:
      | koan                                  | the learner discovers                                                                                                                                                                   | teaches                                                                         | hint                                                                                                                                                                         |
      | Every koan is given a repo            | every koan is given repo, a Plasm Repo whose changes are undone when the koan ends; its Count answers Ok 3L for the three customers                                                     | aggregates: Counting a filtered query                                           | Count the rows of the customers table under Given, and write the number with an L, since a count is an int64.                                                                |
      | ok opens a Result                     | a repo answers with a Result; ok takes the value out of an Ok, so ok (Ok 4L) is 4L                                                                                                      | core: Unsupported translation is explicit                                       | The line above the blank shows what orders is, and ok takes away its Ok.                                                                                                     |
      | A repo pairs a model with a database  | repo holds Db.model and its ten record types, and can check them against the database's tables                                                                                          | schema-check: A model that matches the database passes                          |                                                                                                                                                                              |
      | In your app, you start the repo       | Repo.Start(Db.model, provider, queriesIn = ...) makes and checks a repo, as an app does with Postgres.connect; an unchecked one is written as Ignore; it reads the same three customers | query-check: Queries that translate and a database that fits start a repository | The new repo reads the same database, so count the rows of the customers table under Given.                                                                                  |
      | sqlSent () is the SQL a koan has sent | sqlSent () lists the SQL the koan has sent so far: none at first, one command after a Count; later koans count it to show when Plasm talks to the database                              | core: Query execution exposes diagnostic information                            | The comment says what every koan starts with, and the Count in the middle is a single command.                                                                               |
      | A query is a description              | Query.from builds a value; sqlSent () stays empty until a repo runs it                                                                                                                  | core: Constructing a query performs no database operations                      | The koan's comment says how much building a query sends.                                                                                                                     |
      | The repo shows its SQL                | repo.Explain shows the SQL a repo would send for a query, without sending anything                                                                                                      | elegance: Loading plans can be inspected                                        | The query reads Product, whose table Shop.fs names, and the comment says whether Explain sends anything.                                                                     |
      | Running sends that SQL                | repo.All sends the query as one command, exactly the SQL repo.Explain showed                                                                                                            | core: Query execution exposes diagnostic information                            | Count the repo calls that run a query, which Explain does not, and compare what Explain showed with what All sent.                                                           |
      | A query runs each time you ask        | running the same query twice sends it twice; the query value itself does not change                                                                                                     | core: Executing a query does not mutate its description                         | Each repo.All is a command of its own, and both read the same unchanged rows.                                                                                                |
      | Every call returns a Result           | a count comes back as Ok 4L, and finding no row is Ok None, not a failure                                                                                                               | reading: A query matching no rows returns None                                  | Each is a Result holding what the call read: count the orders table under Given, and look there for a customer named Zed.                                                    |
      | A repo knows only its model           | a repo whose model knows only Product returns an Error naming Customer, and sends nothing                                                                                               | core: Unsupported translation is explicit                                       | The error carries the name of the record type the narrow model was not given, and the comment says the read returns an Error: ask whether such a query reaches the database. |
